--- A#1: fundResidualViaGateway standalone, DCW signer ---
Script: app/scripts/campaign-02-fund-residual-standalone.mts (deleted after use)
Target: 0.10 USDC landing on Arc testnet, source Ethereum_Sepolia, default fee margin (1.20 USDC
deposit). Confirmed Gateway balance before: 1.000000 USDC (leftover from an earlier session's
manual proof).

FIRST RUN: deposited 1.30 USDC for real (confirmed via `cast call balanceOf` on Sepolia USDC:
2,500,000 -> 1,200,000 base units, exactly -1.30 USDC), then the poll loop's `getUsdcBalances`
call threw `NETWORK_GATEWAY_API_ERROR: Maximum retry attempts (10) exceeded: fetch failed` from
inside App Kit's own `getConfirmedDeposits` -- a real, transient Circle Gateway API outage (not a
code bug, not the raw-key-specific RPC issue A#3 step 4 hit first): a plain `getUsdcBalances` call
run moments later succeeded normally, and A#3's raw-key deposit (different signer, same moment)
failed with the identical generic error, ruling out anything specific to one signer path.

REAL, NON-OBVIOUS FINDING for AGENTS.md: `fundResidualViaGateway` is not safely re-callable as a
whole after a mid-flight failure once the deposit leg has already succeeded -- calling it again
would deposit a SECOND time (compounding the ~1.1 USDC fee overhead for no reason). Recovered by
writing a continuation script (app/scripts/campaign-02b-continue-spend-dcw.mts, deleted after use)
that polls `getUsdcBalances` for the already-deposited funds to confirm, then calls `spendOntoArc`
directly -- exactly `fundResidualViaGateway`'s own logic minus the deposit step. A future version
of this function should probably accept a "skip deposit, resume from polling" mode, or the caller
should track whether the deposit leg already succeeded before retrying the whole call. Not fixed
in this campaign (out of scope -- a design change, not a live-proof task), just documented.

CONTINUATION RESULT: confirmed after 11 polls (~5.5 min at the 30s poll interval, well inside the
~10 min CCTP norm), then `spendOntoArc` succeeded for real:
  tx 0xeb98f724689f7a8fcef67025e588d605f3502a264bbf7e5a1e6c2ab67fa59394
  https://testnet.arcscan.app/tx/0xeb98f724689f7a8fcef67025e588d605f3502a264bbf7e5a1e6c2ab67fa59394
Independently verified via `cast receipt`: status 1 (success), `from` is the DCW wallet's own
address, a real `Transfer` log mints exactly 100,000 base units (0.10 USDC) to the DCW wallet.
DCW's Arc-testnet USDC balance: 9,404,944 -> 9,497,448 base units (+92,504, ~0.0925 USDC -- the
small gap from a clean 100,000 is the same minor forwarder-fee split already seen and accepted in
every other Unified Balance proof this project has run).

